CHAPTER I GENERAL PROVISIONS

Article 1 (Purpose)
The purpose of this Decree is to prescribe matters delegated by the Act on Electronic Registration of Stocks, Bonds, etc. and matters necessary for its enforcement.

Article 2 (Scope of Stocks, etc.)
(1) "Rights prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 2, subparagraph 1(l) of the Act on Electronic Registration of Stocks, Bonds, etc. (hereinafter referred to as the "Act") means any of the following rights:
1. Rights represented by securities or certificates under Article 4-3, subparagraph 1 of the Enforcement Decree of the Financial Investment Services and Capital Markets Act;
2. Other rights similar to the rights under subparagraph 1 that are determined and publicly notified by the Financial Services Commission.
(2) "Rights prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 2, subparagraph 1(m) of the Act means rights that may or must be represented by domestically issued securities depositary receipts among the securities depositary receipts under Article 4(8) of the Financial Investment Services and Capital Markets Act.
(3) "Rights prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 2, subparagraph 1(o) of the Act means any of the following rights: <Amended 2023.6.27>
1. Rights that may or must be represented by negotiable certificates of deposit;
2. Rights that must be represented by contingent capital securities under the Banking Act, the Financial Holding Companies Act, or the Insurance Business Act;
3. Other rights determined and publicly notified by the Financial Services Commission, taking into consideration the transferability, fungibility, and other characteristics of the relevant rights.

CHAPTER II SYSTEM OPERATING INSTITUTIONS

Article 3 (Requirements, etc. for Electronic Registration Business Licenses)
(1) "Business units prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 5(1) of the Act means the licensed business units for electronic registration business specified in attached Table 1.
(2) "Amount prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 5(2)2 of the Act means the minimum amount of equity capital for each licensed business unit for electronic registration business specified in attached Table 1.
(3) The business plan under Article 5(2)3 of the Act shall include all the following matters:
1. Provisions on matters necessary for the stable conduct of electronic registration business (meaning the business of conducting the activities referred to in the subparagraphs of Article 14(1) of the Act; hereinafter the same shall apply);
2. Provisions on appropriate internal control mechanisms for risk management, prevention of financial incidents, and other related matters;
3. Provisions on business methods for protecting right holders;
4. Provisions on the accumulation and management of financial resources necessary to ensure the safety of electronic registration, including the resolution of excess amounts under Article 42 of the Act;
5. Other contents of the business plan shall not violate statutes or regulations or be likely to undermine sound transaction practices.
(4) Details concerning personnel, computer equipment, and other physical facilities under Article 5(2)4 of the Act shall be as follows:
1. The necessary personnel, including computer personnel capable of performing the electronic registration business to be conducted, shall be adequately secured;
2. All the following physical facilities, including computer equipment, shall be provided:
(a) Computer equipment and means of communication necessary to perform electronic registration business;
(b) Sufficient work space, including offices, and office equipment;
(c) Security facilities capable of safely protecting physical facilities, including computer equipment;
(d) Supplementary facilities necessary to maintain business continuity in the event of power outages, fires, or other incidents.
(5) The capacity to make capital contributions, financial condition, and social credibility of major shareholders under Article 5(2)7 of the Act (meaning major shareholders under Article 12(2)6(a) of the Financial Investment Services and Capital Markets Act; hereinafter the same shall apply) shall meet the requirements in attached Table 2.
(6) "Social credibility prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 5(2)8 of the Act means compliance with all the following requirements. Provided, That cases where the extent of a violation or the like is deemed minor shall be excluded.
1. There shall have been no criminal punishment under joint penalty provisions during the most recent three years for violations of statutes or regulations under Article 5 of the Enforcement Decree of the Act on Corporate Governance of Financial Companies (hereinafter referred to as "financial statutes and regulations"), the Monopoly Regulation and Fair Trade Act, or the Punishment of Tax Offenses Act;
2. There shall have been no undermining of sound transaction practices through default on obligations or the like during the most recent three years;
3. The person shall not have been designated an insolvent financial institution under the Act on the Structural Improvement of the Financial Industry or had a business permission, authorization, or registration revoked under financial statutes and regulations during the most recent five years;
4. After receiving from the Financial Services Commission, a foreign financial supervisory authority, or the like, pursuant to financial statutes and regulations or foreign financial statutes and regulations (meaning foreign financial statutes and regulations corresponding to financial statutes and regulations), a measure at least as severe as the closure of a branch or other business office or the suspension of all or part of its business (including an equivalent administrative disposition; hereinafter the same shall apply in this subparagraph), the following applicable period shall have elapsed:
(a) Suspension of all business: Three years from the date on which the suspension ends;
(b) Suspension of part of the business: Two years from the date on which the suspension ends;
(c) Closure of a branch or other business office or suspension of all or part of its business: One year from the date of the measure.
(7) The system for preventing conflicts of interest under Article 5(2)9 of the Act (hereinafter referred to as the "system for preventing conflicts of interest") shall be a system that identifies and assesses the likelihood of conflicts of interest arising between an electronic registration institution and account management institutions, etc. under Article 23(1) of the Act, or among the businesses conducted by the electronic registration institution, in connection with the conduct of electronic registration business, and appropriately manages such conflicts in accordance with the methods and procedures prescribed in the electronic registration institution's internal control standards.
(8) The Financial Services Commission and the Minister of Justice may jointly determine and publicly notify specific standards necessary for the licensing requirements under paragraphs (3) through (7).

Article 4 (Methods and Procedures for Electronic Registration Business Licensing)
(1) A person intending to obtain an electronic registration business license pursuant to Article 6(1) of the Act shall submit an application for a license stating the following matters to the Financial Services Commission and the Minister of Justice:
1. Name;
2. Locations of the head office, branches, and other business offices;
3. Matters concerning officers;
4. Matters concerning the licensed business units for electronic registration business to be conducted (meaning the licensed business units for electronic registration business under Article 5(1) of the Act; hereinafter the same shall apply);
5. Other matters necessary for examining the requirements for an electronic registration business license that are jointly determined and publicly notified by the Financial Services Commission and the Minister of Justice.
(2) The following documents shall accompany the application for a license under paragraph (1):
1. Articles of incorporation;
2. Documents evidencing decisions on establishment or application for a license, such as minutes of a general meeting of promoters, an inaugural general meeting of shareholders, or a meeting of the board of directors;
3. A document stating the locations and names of the head office, branches, and other business offices;
4. Resumes and certificates of career experience of officers;
5. A document stating the types of licensed business units for electronic registration business and business methods;
6. Financial statements for the most recent three business years and their accompanying schedules (excluding corporations in the process of establishment; for a corporation for which three business years have not elapsed since its establishment, this means financial statements and their accompanying schedules from the date of establishment through the most recent business year);
7. A business plan for the three business years following commencement of business (including projected financial statements) and a statement of projected income and expenditure;
8. Documents enabling verification of the status of personnel, computer equipment, and other physical facilities;
9. A document stating the personal names or corporate names of shareholders owning at least 1 percent of the total number of issued shares as of the date of the application for a license (the last day of the most recent business year in the case of an application for a license to add licensed business units for electronic registration business) and the numbers of shares they own;
10. Documents enabling verification that major shareholders meet the requirements under Article 5(2)7 of the Act;
11. Documents enabling verification of whether a system for preventing conflicts of interest is in place;
12. Other documents necessary for examining the licensing requirements that are jointly determined and publicly notified by the Financial Services Commission and the Minister of Justice.
(3) Notwithstanding paragraphs (1) and (2), where a person intending to obtain an electronic registration business license has applied for a preliminary license under Article 7(1) of the Act, and the contents of the preliminary license application and accompanying documents submitted at the time of that application have not changed by the time of the application for a license under Article 6(1) of the Act, the person may omit some of the matters to be stated in the application for a license under paragraph (1) or omit submission of the corresponding accompanying documents under paragraph (2) by specifically identifying the relevant portions and stating that reference should be made to them.
(4) Upon receiving an application for a license under paragraph (1), the Financial Services Commission and the Minister of Justice shall verify the certificate of registered corporate matters through the joint use of administrative information under Article 36(1) of the Electronic Government Act.
(5) Upon receiving an application for a license under paragraph (1), the Financial Services Commission and the Minister of Justice shall verify the factual accuracy of the application for an electronic registration business license and examine whether the person applying for the electronic registration business license (hereinafter referred to as the "license applicant" in this Article) meets the licensing requirements under Article 5(2) of the Act.
(6) Where necessary to verify the contents of an application for an electronic registration business license pursuant to paragraph (5), the Financial Services Commission and the Minister of Justice may conduct an on-site investigation through interviews with interested parties, promoters, or officers, or by other means.
(7) To gather opinions from interested parties and others on the contents of an application for an electronic registration business license, the Financial Services Commission and the Minister of Justice shall publicly announce the following matters on the websites of the Financial Services Commission and the Ministry of Justice or by other means:
1. The name of the applicant for an electronic registration business license;
2. The date of the application for an electronic registration business license;
3. The contents of the application for an electronic registration business license;
4. Matters concerning procedures for presenting opinions, including the methods and period for presenting opinions on whether an electronic registration business license should be granted.
(8) Where, as a result of gathering opinions from interested parties and others pursuant to paragraph (7), there are opinions deemed unfavorable to the license applicant, the Financial Services Commission and the Minister of Justice may notify the license applicant of those opinions and require the applicant to provide an explanation by a specified deadline.
(9) Where deemed necessary for examining an electronic registration business license, the Financial Services Commission and the Minister of Justice may hold a public hearing.
(10) A person who has obtained an electronic registration business license pursuant to Article 6(2) of the Act shall commence the licensed electronic registration business within six months from the date on which the license is obtained. Provided, That where the Financial Services Commission and the Minister of Justice separately set the deadline or extend the deadline upon application by the person who has obtained the electronic registration business license, that person may commence the licensed electronic registration business within that deadline.
(11) Where the Financial Services Commission and the Minister of Justice attach conditions to an electronic registration business license, they shall verify compliance with those conditions.
(12) Except as provided in paragraphs (1) through (11), matters necessary for applications for and examination of electronic registration business licenses, the form and method of preparing applications for a license, and other related matters shall be jointly determined and publicly notified by the Financial Services Commission and the Minister of Justice.

Article 5 (Periods Excluded from the License Examination Period)
"Periods prescribed by Presidential Decree, including the period for remedying deficiencies in a license application" in Article 6(3) of the Act means any of the following periods:
1. The period required for the Financial Services Commission and the Minister of Justice to obtain necessary materials from other institutions or the like to verify whether a person intending to obtain an electronic registration business license meets the requirements in the subparagraphs of Article 5(2) of the Act;
2. Where the Financial Services Commission and the Minister of Justice request that deficiencies in an application for a license under Article 6(1) of the Act be remedied pursuant to the latter part of Article 6(2) of the Act, the period for remedying those deficiencies;
3. Where criminal proceedings against a person intending to obtain an electronic registration business license or a major shareholder of such a person are ongoing, or procedures such as investigations or inspections by the Ministry of Justice, the Fair Trade Commission, the Financial Services Commission, the National Tax Service, a prosecutors' office, the Financial Supervisory Service under the Act on the Establishment of the Financial Services Commission (hereinafter referred to as the "Financial Supervisory Service"), or the like are ongoing, and the subject matter of those proceedings, investigations, inspections, or the like is deemed capable of materially affecting examination of the electronic registration business license, the period until those proceedings, investigations, inspections, or other procedures are concluded.

Article 6 (Methods and Procedures, etc. for Preliminary Licensing)
(1) A person intending to apply for a preliminary license pursuant to Article 7(1) of the Act shall submit an application for a preliminary license stating the matters referred to in the subparagraphs of Article 4(1) to the Financial Services Commission and the Minister of Justice.
(2) The following documents shall accompany the application for a preliminary license under paragraph (1):
1. Articles of incorporation or draft articles of incorporation;
2. Documents evidencing decisions on establishment or application for a license, such as minutes of a general meeting of promoters, an inaugural general meeting of shareholders, or a meeting of the board of directors;
3. Resumes and certificates of career experience of officers (including persons scheduled to be appointed as officers);
4. A document stating the types of licensed business units for electronic registration business to be conducted and business methods;
5. Financial statements for the most recent three business years and their accompanying schedules (excluding corporations in the process of establishment; for a corporation for which three business years have not elapsed since its establishment, this means financial statements and their accompanying schedules from the date of establishment through the most recent business year);
6. A business plan for the three business years following commencement of business (including projected financial statements);
7. Documents enabling verification of the status of personnel, computer equipment, other physical facilities, etc. (including personnel scheduled to be hired, physical facilities scheduled to be purchased, and the like);
8. A document stating the personal names or corporate names of shareholders owning at least 1 percent of the total number of issued shares as of the date of application for a preliminary license (the last day of the most recent business year in the case of an application for a preliminary license to add licensed business units for electronic registration business) and the numbers of shares they own;
9. Documents enabling verification that major shareholders meet the requirements under Article 5(2)7 of the Act;
10. Documents enabling verification of whether a system for preventing conflicts of interest is in place or can be established;
11. Other documents necessary for examining a preliminary license under Article 7 of the Act that are jointly determined and publicly notified by the Financial Services Commission and the Minister of Justice.
(3) Article 4(4) through (9) shall apply mutatis mutandis to the methods and procedures for examining a preliminary license applied for pursuant to Article 7(1) of the Act. In such cases, "application for a license" shall each be construed as "application for a preliminary license," and "electronic registration business license" shall each be construed as "preliminary license."
(4) A person who has obtained a preliminary license pursuant to Article 7(2) of the Act shall fulfill the contents and conditions of the preliminary license and apply for an electronic registration business license under Article 5 of the Act (hereinafter referred to as a "final license" in this paragraph) within six months from the date on which the preliminary license is obtained. Provided, That where the Financial Services Commission and the Minister of Justice separately set a deadline for applying for a final license at the time of the preliminary license, or extend that deadline after the preliminary license upon application by the person who has obtained it, that person may apply for a final license within that deadline.
(5) Except as provided in paragraphs (1) through (4), matters necessary for applications for and examination of preliminary licenses, the form and method of preparing applications for a preliminary license, and other related matters shall be jointly determined and publicly notified by the Financial Services Commission and the Minister of Justice.

Article 7 (Periods Excluded from the Preliminary License Examination Period)
"Periods prescribed by Presidential Decree, including the period for remedying deficiencies related to an application for a preliminary license" in Article 7(3) of the Act means any of the following periods:
1. The period required for the Financial Services Commission and the Minister of Justice to obtain necessary materials from other institutions or the like to verify whether a person who has applied for a preliminary license pursuant to Article 7(1) of the Act can meet the requirements in the subparagraphs of Article 5(2) of the Act;
2. Where the Financial Services Commission and the Minister of Justice request that deficiencies relating to an application for a preliminary license be remedied pursuant to the latter part of Article 7(2) of the Act, the period for remedying those deficiencies;
3. Where criminal proceedings against a person who has applied for a preliminary license pursuant to Article 7(1) of the Act or a major shareholder of such a person are ongoing, or procedures such as investigations or inspections by the Ministry of Justice, the Fair Trade Commission, the Financial Services Commission, the National Tax Service, a prosecutors' office, the Financial Supervisory Service, or the like are ongoing, and the subject matter of those proceedings, investigations, inspections, or the like is deemed capable of materially affecting examination of the preliminary license under Article 7(2) of the Act, the period until those proceedings, investigations, inspections, or other procedures are concluded.

Article 8 (Approval for Discontinuance, etc. of Electronic Registration Business)
(1) Where an electronic registration institution intends to obtain approval for discontinuance of all or part of its electronic registration business or dissolution of the electronic registration institution (hereinafter referred to as "discontinuance, etc." in this Article) pursuant to the former part of Article 12(1) of the Act, it shall submit an application for approval stating the following matters to the Financial Services Commission:
1. Name;
2. Location of the head office;
3. Matters concerning officers;
4. The reasons for, contents of, and timing of the application for approval, and other related matters;
5. Other matters necessary for examining the approval that are determined and publicly notified by the Financial Services Commission.
(2) The following documents shall accompany the application for approval under paragraph (1):
1. Articles of incorporation;
2. Where a resolution of the board of directors or a general meeting of shareholders has been adopted concerning the reasons for applying for approval for discontinuance, etc., the relevant minutes;
3. Where a contract relating to the reasons for applying for approval for discontinuance, etc. exists, a copy of that contract;
4. Other documents necessary for examining approval for discontinuance, etc. that are determined and publicly notified by the Financial Services Commission.
(3) Where the Financial Services Commission intends to approve discontinuance, etc. pursuant to Article 12(1) of the Act, it shall examine whether all the following criteria are met:
1. The discontinuance, etc. shall be unavoidable in light of the management, financial condition, and other circumstances of the relevant electronic registration institution;
2. The discontinuance, etc. shall not impede the protection of right holders or the maintenance of orderly transactions;
3. There shall be no impediment to following the procedures under the Commercial Act, the Financial Investment Services and Capital Markets Act, and other relevant statutes and regulations.
(4) Upon receipt of an application for approval and accompanying documents under paragraphs (1) and (2) (hereinafter referred to as "approval application documents"), the Financial Services Commission shall examine their contents, decide whether to grant approval within two months from the date of receipt of the approval application documents, and notify the applicant in writing of the result and reasons without delay. In such cases, where there are deficiencies in the approval application documents, the Financial Services Commission may set a deadline and request that they be remedied.
(5) In calculating the examination period under the former part of paragraph (4), periods determined and publicly notified by the Financial Services Commission, including the period for remedying deficiencies in approval application documents under the latter part of that paragraph, shall not be included in the examination period.
(6) Except as provided in paragraphs (1) through (5), matters necessary for applications for and examination of approval for discontinuance, etc., the form and method of preparing applications for approval, and other related matters shall be determined and publicly notified by the Financial Services Commission.

Article 9 (Grounds for Requiring Dismissal of the Representative Director)
"Cases prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the former part of Article 13(4) of the Act means cases where the Financial Services Commission, as a result of reviewing the suitability of the representative director of an electronic registration institution by comprehensively taking into consideration the director's ability to perform duties, expertise, career experience, and other relevant factors, deems the director unsuitable to perform those duties.

Article 10 (Special Interests)
"Special interests prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 13(5) of the Act means any of the following:
1. Guarantees of obligations;
2. Provision of collateral;
3. Interests that cannot be regarded as falling within acts necessary in the course of normal transaction activities (meaning acts related to the content of the counterparty's business or incidental to the achievement of its business purposes that may be recognized as ordinary transaction activities under generally accepted social norms in light of the terms of the transactions and other relevant factors).

Article 11 (Account Management Institutions)
(1) "Persons prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 19, subparagraph 7 of the Act means any of the following persons: <Amended 2022.2.17>
1. The Korea Asset Management Corporation under the Act on the Establishment of Korea Asset Management Corporation;
2. A resolution financial company under Article 36-3(1) of the Depositor Protection Act;
3. The relevant project implementer where compensation bonds under Article 72(1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act are held with that project implementer serving as the account management institution pursuant to paragraph (3) of that Article;
4. Other persons who need to manage customer accounts under Article 22(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "customer accounts") to perform activities under other statutes or regulations and whom the Financial Services Commission designates and publicly notifies as account management institutions.
(2) "Persons prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 19, subparagraph 8 of the Act means any of the following persons:
1. Securities finance companies and merchant banks under the Financial Investment Services and Capital Markets Act;
2. Specialized credit finance companies under the Specialized Credit Finance Business Act;
3. The Export-Import Bank of Korea under the Export-Import Bank of Korea Act;
4. Mutual savings banks and the Korea Federation of Savings Banks under the Mutual Savings Banks Act;
5. Fisheries cooperatives, the National Federation of Fisheries Cooperatives, and Suhyup Bank under the Fisheries Cooperatives Act;
6. Agricultural cooperatives and the National Agricultural Cooperative Federation under the Agricultural Cooperatives Act;
7. Credit unions and the National Credit Union Federation under the Credit Unions Act;
8. Community credit cooperatives and the National Federation of Community Credit Cooperatives under the Community Credit Cooperatives Act;
9. Postal service offices under the Postal Savings and Insurance Act;
10. Electronic registration institutions;
11. Other persons whom the Financial Services Commission designates and publicly notifies as account management institutions, taking into consideration the nature of their activities and other relevant factors.

CHAPTER III OPENING OF ACCOUNTS, ETC.

Article 12 (Opening, etc. of Issuer Management Accounts)
(1) "Securities or certificates prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 21(1)2 of the Act means any of the following:
1. Securities or certificates representing rights falling under subparagraphs 1(b) through 1(e) or 1(k) of Article 2 of the Act [limited to those not listed on a securities market under Article 8-2(4)1 of the Financial Investment Services and Capital Markets Act (hereinafter referred to as a "securities market"), but including those registered with a registration institution under Article 3 of the former Public and Corporate Bond Registration Act (meaning that Act before its repeal by Act No. 14096) without issuing corporate bond certificates];
2. Securities or certificates in registered form representing rights under Article 2, subparagraph 1(g) of the Act.
(2) "Persons prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 21(1)3 of the Act means any of the following foreign corporations, etc. (meaning foreign corporations, etc. under Article 2, subparagraph 1(n) of the Act; hereinafter the same shall apply in this paragraph):
1. Foreign corporations, etc. intending to newly issue stock certificates in Korea;
2. Foreign corporations, etc. that have already issued stock certificates in Korea and intend to have the right holders of those stock certificates hold or acquire stocks by electronic registration.
(3) "Information prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 21(2)1 of the Act means the following information concerning an issuer (meaning a person falling under any of the subparagraphs of paragraph (1) of that Article who has opened an issuer management account pursuant to that paragraph; hereinafter the same shall apply):
1. The issuer's corporate registration number or unique identification number;
2. Locations of the issuer's head office, branches, and other business offices;
3. The year, month, and day of the issuer's establishment, its type of business, the name of its representative, and other equivalent information.
(4) "Matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 21(2)3 of the Act means the following matters:
1. The grounds for electronic registration;
2. The issue date and method of issuance of electronically registered stocks, etc.;
3. In the case of rights under subparagraph 1(b) or 1(e) of Article 2 of the Act that satisfy all the requirements in the subparagraphs of Article 59 of the Act and have been electronically registered (hereinafter referred to as "short-term bonds, etc."), their issuance limit and unredeemed outstanding balance;
4. Other matters prescribed by an electronic registration institution in its electronic registration business rules under Article 15 of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "electronic registration business rules").

Article 13 (Registers Taking Precedence over Issuer Management Account Registers)
"Registers prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 21(3)4 of the Act means the following registers:
1. A corporate bond register under Article 488 of the Commercial Act;
2. A trust bond register under Article 87(4) of the Trust Act;
3. A register of local government bond certificates under Article 12 of the Local Finance Act.

Article 14 (Matters to Be Electronically Registered in Customer Account Registers)
"Matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 22(2)7 of the Act means, where the quantity or amount of electronically registered stocks, etc. electronically registered in a customer account register under that paragraph (hereinafter referred to as a "customer account register") increases or decreases, the reason for that increase or decrease.

Article 15 (Matters to Be Recorded in Customer Management Account Registers)
"Matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 22(4)3 of the Act means, where the quantity or amount of electronically registered stocks, etc. recorded in a customer management account register under that paragraph (hereinafter referred to as a "customer management account register") increases or decreases, the reason for that increase or decrease.

Article 16 (Scope of Persons Opening Proprietary Accounts of Account Management Institutions, etc.)
"Persons prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 23(1) of the Act means any of the following persons:
1. Corporations managing and operating funds established pursuant to Acts;
2. Individuals, corporations, or organizations determined and publicly notified by the Financial Services Commission, taking into consideration the size and purpose of their holdings of stocks, etc., the types of the relevant stocks, etc., and other relevant factors.

Article 17 (Matters to Be Electronically Registered in Proprietary Account Registers of Account Management Institutions, etc.)
"Matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 23(2)3 of the Act means, where the quantity or amount of electronically registered stocks, etc. electronically registered in a proprietary account register of account management institutions, etc. under that paragraph (hereinafter referred to as a "proprietary account register of account management institutions, etc.") increases or decreases, the reason for that increase or decrease.

Chapter IV Electronic Registration

Article 18 (New Electronic Registration of Stocks, etc.)
(1) "Stocks, etc. prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 25(1)3 of the Act means any of the following: <Amended on June 27, 2023>
1. Stocks, etc. falling under either of the following, among the stocks, etc. referred to in subparagraph 1(b) of Article 2 of the Act:
(a) Rights required to be represented by contingent capital securities under the Financial Investment Services and Capital Markets Act;
(b) Bonds referred to in Article 469(2)3 of the Commercial Act (limited to cases where the issuer is an investment trader under the Financial Investment Services and Capital Markets Act);
2. Rights referred to in subparagraph 1(j), (l), or (m) of Article 2 of the Act;
3. Rights required to be represented by contingent capital securities under the Banking Act, the Financial Holding Companies Act, and the Insurance Business Act;
4. Other rights prescribed and publicly notified by the Financial Services Commission as stocks, etc. for which it is necessary to apply for new electronic registration in consideration of the structure of issuance and circulation of stocks, etc., the substance and methods of the exercise of rights by right holders of stocks, etc., and other relevant matters.
(2) "Cases prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 25(2) of the Act means cases where an issuer applies to an electronic registration institution for electronic registration for the first time for each issue of the relevant stocks, etc.

Article 19 (Methods and Procedures for Applications for Electronic Registration, etc.)
(1) Where an issuer applies to an electronic registration institution for new electronic registration or prior examination pursuant to Article 25(1) or (2) of the Act, the issuer must submit an application for electronic registration or an application for prior examination (hereinafter referred to as an "electronic registration application, etc.") stating the following matters pursuant to the former part of paragraph (3) of that Article:
1. The name of the issuer;
2. The type, issue, and quantity or amount by issue of the stocks, etc. for which new electronic registration or prior examination is requested pursuant to Article 25(1) or (2) of the Act;
3. Other matters required by the electronic registration business rules to be stated in an electronic registration application, etc. for stocks, etc.
(2) The following documents must be attached to an electronic registration application, etc.:
1. Documents according to the following classifications:
(a) In the case of stocks, etc. electronically registered pursuant to Article 356-2, 420-4, 478(3), or 516-7 of the Commercial Act: The articles of incorporation of the issuer of the relevant stocks, etc.;
(b) In the case of other stocks, etc.: A contract, terms and conditions, or an equivalent instrument relating to the issuance of the relevant stocks, etc. that constitutes the basis for issuing the stocks, etc.;
2. A certificate of corporate seal impression and a certificate of registered corporate matters;
3. Other documents prescribed by the electronic registration business rules as necessary for new electronic registration or prior examination of stocks, etc.
(3) An electronic registration institution that receives an electronic registration application, etc. must verify whether the particulars of the application are true and review whether any ground for refusing new electronic registration of stocks, etc. under Article 25(6) of the Act applies.
(4) Matters necessary for the methods of application for and review of new electronic registration or prior examination, the forms of electronic registration applications, etc. and the methods of preparing them, and other relevant matters, other than those provided for in paragraphs (1) through (3), shall be prescribed by the electronic registration business rules.

Article 20 (Periods Not Counted in the Review Period)
"Periods prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 25(5) of the Act means any of the following periods:
1. The period required for an electronic registration institution to obtain necessary materials from other institutions, etc. in order to verify the matters stated in an electronic registration application, etc.;
2. Where an electronic registration institution requests that deficiencies in an electronic registration application, etc. be rectified pursuant to the latter part of Article 25(4) of the Act, the period for such rectification.

Article 21 (Grounds for Refusing New Electronic Registration)
(1) "Cases prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 25(6)1(c) of the Act means any of the following cases:
1. Where it is difficult to exercise rights through an electronic registration institution pursuant to Article 38(1) of the Act;
2. Where the articles of incorporation, contract, terms and conditions, etc. specified in the relevant item below prohibit or restrict the transfer of stocks, etc. according to the following classifications:
(a) Stocks, etc. electronically registered pursuant to Article 356-2, 420-4, 478(3), or 516-7 of the Commercial Act: The articles of incorporation of the issuer of the relevant stocks, etc.;
(b) Other stocks, etc.: A contract, terms and conditions, or an equivalent instrument relating to the issuance of the relevant stocks, etc. that constitutes the basis for issuing the stocks, etc.;
3. Other cases prescribed and publicly notified by the Financial Services Commission where new electronic registration of stocks, etc. is inappropriate in consideration of their fungibility or negotiability, the methods of exercising rights, and other relevant matters.
(2) "Cases prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 25(6)6 of the Act means any of the following cases:
1. Where an issuer applying for new electronic registration of stocks has not appointed a transfer agent company (meaning a person registered pursuant to Article 365(1) of the Financial Investment Services and Capital Markets Act; hereinafter the same shall apply);
2. Other cases prescribed and publicly notified by the Financial Services Commission as necessary for the protection of right holders and the maintenance of order in transactions, such as where an issuer fails to comply with matters or procedures necessary for the protection of right holders when issuing and electronically registering stocks, etc.

Article 22 (Public Announcement and Notification upon Electronic Registration)
(1) "Books prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the part, other than the subparagraphs, of Article 27(1) of the Act means any of the following:
1. The register referred to in Article 21(3)3 of the Act;
2. Books referred to in the subparagraphs of Article 13;
3. The register of beneficiaries referred to in Article 79(1) of the Trust Act.
(2) When making a public announcement pursuant to Article 27(1) of the Act, an issuer must use the method specified in the basis for issuing stocks, etc. according to the following classifications. In such cases, the issuer must also publicly announce the contents on the website of the electronic registration institution:
1. In the case of stocks, etc. electronically registered pursuant to Article 356-2, 420-4, 478(3), or 516-7 of the Commercial Act: The articles of incorporation of the issuer of the relevant stocks, etc.;
2. In the case of other stocks, etc.: A contract, terms and conditions, or an equivalent instrument relating to the issuance of the relevant stocks, etc. that constitutes the basis for issuing the stocks, etc.
(3) Where an issuer gives notification pursuant to Article 27(1) of the Act, the issuer must give written notification at least once.

Article 23 (Methods and Procedures for Additional Applications for New Electronic Registration, etc.)
(1) Where an issuer intends to make an additional application for new electronic registration pursuant to Article 27(2) of the Act, the issuer must submit to the electronic registration institution an application for additional electronic registration stating the following matters:
1. The name of the issuer;
2. The type, issue, and quantity or amount by issue of the stocks, etc. to be additionally electronically registered;
3. The name of the person that opened the customer account or the proprietary account of account management institutions, etc. under Article 23(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as a "proprietary account of account management institutions, etc.") in which the stocks, etc. are to be additionally electronically registered;
4. The customer account or proprietary account of account management institutions, etc. in which the stocks, etc. are to be additionally electronically registered (hereinafter referred to as an "electronic registration account"), and the quantity or amount of stocks, etc. for each electronic registration account;
5. The grounds for the additional application for new electronic registration;
6. Other matters required by the electronic registration business rules to be stated in an application for additional electronic registration.
(2) The following documents must be attached to an application for additional electronic registration under paragraph (1):
1. Documents according to the following classifications:
(a) In the case of stocks, etc. electronically registered pursuant to Article 356-2, 420-4, 478(3), or 516-7 of the Commercial Act: The articles of incorporation of the issuer of the relevant stocks, etc.;
(b) In the case of other stocks, etc.: A contract, terms and conditions, or an equivalent instrument relating to the issuance of the relevant stocks, etc. that constitutes the basis for issuing the stocks, etc.;
2. A certificate of corporate seal impression and a certificate of registered corporate matters;
3. Other documents prescribed by the electronic registration business rules as documents to be attached to an additional application for new electronic registration of stocks, etc.
(3) An electronic registration institution that receives an application for additional electronic registration pursuant to paragraph (1) must verify whether the particulars of the application are true and review whether any ground for refusing new electronic registration of stocks, etc. under the subparagraphs of Article 25(6) of the Act applies.
(4) Matters necessary for additional applications for new electronic registration of stocks, etc., the methods of reviewing grounds for refusal, the form of an application for additional electronic registration and the method of preparing it, and other relevant matters, other than those provided for in paragraphs (1) through (3), shall be prescribed by the electronic registration business rules.

Article 24 (Opening and Management of Special Accounts)
(1) "Institution prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 29(1) of the Act means an electronic registration institution.
(2) "Cases prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 29(2)4 of the Act means any of the following cases:
1. Where stocks, etc. electronically registered in an electronic registration account under Article 29(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as a "special account") are transferred pursuant to a comprehensive exchange of stocks under Article 360-2 of the Commercial Act or a comprehensive transfer of stocks under Article 360-15 of that Act;
2. Where stocks, etc. electronically registered in a special account are transferred pursuant to a controlling shareholder's demand for sale under Article 360-24 of the Commercial Act;
3. Where, as a result of exercising rights attached to stocks electronically registered in a special account with the Korea Securities Depository under Article 294 of the Financial Investment Services and Capital Markets Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Korea Securities Depository") named as their owner, the Korea Securities Depository has received stocks from the issuer, and the purpose is to sell the stocks received, after one year has elapsed from the date of receipt, through the securities market, etc. and manage them in cash: Provided, That in cases prescribed and publicly notified by the Financial Services Commission, such as where the issuer of the relevant stocks is delisted, the stocks may be sold through the securities market, etc. even before one year has elapsed from the date of receipt;
4. Other cases prescribed and publicly notified by the Financial Services Commission where it is necessary to transfer stocks, etc. electronically registered in a special account and there is no risk of harming the interests of the right holders of the relevant stocks, etc., such as compulsory execution under the Civil Execution Act.
(3) "Grounds prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the proviso to Article 29(3) of the Act means any of the following cases:
1. Where electronically registered treasury stock and other stocks, etc. are transferred to a special account pursuant to the issuer's merger, division, or merger after division;
2. Where electronically registered stocks, etc. are transferred to a special account as consideration for a company's acquisition of redeemable stocks pursuant to Article 345(4) of the Commercial Act;
3. Where electronically registered treasury stock and other stocks, etc. of a company that becomes a wholly owning parent company pursuant to a comprehensive exchange of stocks under Article 360-2 of the Commercial Act are transferred to a special account;
4. Where treasury stock and other stocks, etc. are transferred to a special account in order to pay dividends in kind under Article 462-4(1) of the Commercial Act;
5. Other cases prescribed and publicly notified by the Financial Services Commission where it is necessary to transfer electronically registered stocks, etc. to a special account.

Article 25 (Methods of Applying for Electronic Registration of Transfers between Accounts, etc.)
(1) "Cases prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 30(1)3 of the Act means any of the following cases:
1. Where the owner of electronically registered stocks, etc. has been issued a document certifying the electronic registration of electronically registered stocks, etc. pursuant to Article 63(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as an "electronic registration certificate"), and either of the following persons who has received that electronic registration certificate from the owner of the electronically registered stocks, etc. transfers the electronically registered stocks, etc. that formed the basis for issuing the electronic registration certificate to that person's own electronic registration account:
(a) Where the owner of electronically registered stocks, etc. has deposited the electronically registered stocks, etc. pursuant to the Deposit Act, the person to receive the deposited property;
(b) Where the owner of electronically registered stocks, etc. has paid the electronically registered stocks, etc. in lieu of a security deposit or deposit money payable pursuant to Article 171 of the Financial Investment Services and Capital Markets Act, the person who received the electronically registered stocks, etc. as payment;
2. Where a person who intends to acquire rights to electronically registered stocks, etc. pursuant to a court judgment (including anything having the same effect as a final and conclusive judgment; hereinafter the same shall apply), decision, or order transfers the electronically registered stocks, etc. to that person's own electronic registration account;
3. Other cases prescribed and publicly notified by the Financial Services Commission where it is recognized that a transfer of electronically registered stocks, etc. is necessary.
(2) A person who intends to transfer electronically registered stocks, etc. pursuant to Article 30(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as the "transferor" in this Article) must apply for electronic registration of a transfer between accounts to the electronic registration institution or account management institution with which the relevant electronically registered stocks, etc. are electronically registered, specifying the following matters in detail: Provided, That if the transferor consents, the person who intends to acquire the electronically registered stocks, etc. by transfer (hereinafter referred to as the "transferee" in this Article) may apply for electronic registration of a transfer between accounts, attaching the transferor's written consent:
1. The type, issue, and quantity or amount by issue of the electronically registered stocks, etc. subject to the transfer between accounts;
2. The names of the transferor and the transferee;
3. Other matters prescribed by the electronic registration business rules as necessary for electronic registration of a transfer of electronically registered stocks, etc. between accounts.
(3) Notwithstanding paragraph (2), a person who intends to acquire rights pursuant to a court judgment, decision, or order, or who acquires rights to electronically registered stocks, etc. through universal succession by reason of inheritance, merger, etc., may apply for electronic registration of a transfer between accounts, attaching documents evidencing the acquisition of the rights.
(4) An electronic registration institution or account management institution that receives an application for electronic registration of a transfer between accounts pursuant to paragraph (2) or (3) must, without delay, electronically register the transfer of the relevant electronically registered stocks, etc. between accounts in the proprietary account register of account management institutions, etc. or the customer account register in accordance with the following methods and procedures:
1. In the case of an application for electronic registration of a transfer between proprietary accounts of account management institutions, etc.:
(a) The electronic registration institution must electronically register a decrease in the transferor's proprietary account register of account management institutions, etc.;
(b) The electronic registration institution must electronically register an increase in the transferee's proprietary account register of account management institutions, etc.;
2. In the case of an application for electronic registration of a transfer between customer accounts opened with the same account management institution:
(a) The account management institution must electronically register a decrease in the transferor's customer account register;
(b) The account management institution must electronically register an increase in the transferee's customer account register;
3. In the case of an application for electronic registration of a transfer from a proprietary account of account management institutions, etc. to a customer account:
(a) The electronic registration institution must electronically register a decrease in the transferor's proprietary account register of account management institutions, etc.;
(b) The electronic registration institution must make an entry of an increase in the customer management account register of the account management institution with which the transferee opened a customer account (hereinafter referred to as the "transferee's account management institution" in this Article), and then notify the transferee's account management institution of that fact without delay;
(c) The transferee's account management institution must, without delay, electronically register an increase in the transferee's customer account register in accordance with the notification;
4. In the case of an application for electronic registration of a transfer from a customer account to a proprietary account of account management institutions, etc.:
(a) The account management institution with which the transferor opened a customer account (hereinafter referred to as the "transferor's account management institution" in this Article) must electronically register a decrease in the transferor's customer account register, and then notify the electronic registration institution of that fact without delay;
(b) The electronic registration institution must, without delay, make an entry of a decrease in the customer management account register of the transferor's account management institution in accordance with the notification;
(c) The electronic registration institution must electronically register an increase in the transferee's proprietary account register of account management institutions, etc.;
5. In the case of an application for electronic registration of a transfer between customer accounts opened with different account management institutions:
(a) The transferor's account management institution must electronically register a decrease in the transferor's customer account register, and then notify the electronic registration institution of that fact without delay;
(b) The electronic registration institution must, without delay, make an entry of a decrease in the customer management account register of the transferor's account management institution in accordance with the notification;
(c) The electronic registration institution must make an entry of an increase in the customer management account register of the transferee's account management institution, and then notify the transferee's account management institution of that fact without delay;
(d) The transferee's account management institution must, without delay, electronically register an increase in the transferee's customer account register in accordance with the notification.

Article 26 (Methods of Applying for Electronic Registration of the Establishment and Cancellation of Pledges, etc.)
(1) An application for electronic registration of the establishment of a pledge under Article 31(1) of the Act must be made by the pledgor: Provided, That if the pledgor consents, the pledgee may apply for electronic registration of the establishment of a pledge, attaching the pledgor's written consent.
(2) An application for electronic registration of the cancellation of a pledge under Article 31(1) of the Act must be made by the pledgee: Provided, That if the pledgee consents, the pledgor may apply for electronic registration of the cancellation of a pledge, attaching the pledgee's written consent.
(3) A person who intends to establish or cancel a pledge over electronically registered stocks, etc. pursuant to paragraph (1) or (2) must apply for electronic registration of the establishment or cancellation of the pledge to the electronic registration institution or account management institution with which the relevant electronically registered stocks, etc. are electronically registered, specifying the following matters in detail:
1. The type, issue, and quantity or amount by issue of the relevant electronically registered stocks, etc.;
2. The names of the pledgor and the pledgee;
3. Other matters prescribed by the electronic registration business rules as necessary for electronic registration of the establishment and cancellation of a pledge over electronically registered stocks, etc.

Article 27 (Methods of Applying for Electronic Registration Indicating Status as Trust Property and Cancelling Such Indication, etc.)
(1) An application for electronic registration indicating the fact that property is trust property under Article 32(1) of the Act must be made by the person according to the following classifications:
1. Where electronically registered stocks, etc. become part of trust property pursuant to an application for electronic registration of a transfer from the settlor's electronic registration account to the trustee's electronic registration account: The settlor;
2. Where electronically registered stocks, etc. become part of trust property by a method other than that under subparagraph 1: The trustee.
(2) Electronic registration cancelling the indication of the fact that property is trust property under Article 32(1) of the Act must be applied for by the trustee.
(3) A person applying for electronic registration indicating the fact that property is trust property or cancelling such indication pursuant to paragraph (1) or (2) must apply for electronic registration to the electronic registration institution or account management institution with which the relevant electronically registered stocks, etc. are electronically registered, specifying the following matters in detail:
1. The type, issue, and quantity or amount by issue of the relevant electronically registered stocks, etc.;
2. The name of the trustee;
3. Other matters prescribed by the electronic registration business rules as necessary for electronic registration indicating the fact that electronically registered stocks, etc. are trust property and cancelling such indication.
(4) Electronic registration indicating the fact that property is trust property or cancelling such indication must be made in the trustee's proprietary account register of account management institutions, etc. or customer account register.

Article 28 (Electronic Registration of Modifications and Cancellations upon Application)
(1) "Grounds prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 33(1)5 of the Act means any of the following cases:
1. Where the issuer has been dissolved or liquidated pursuant to the Commercial Act or other statutes;
2. Where there is a court judgment, decision, or order;
3. Where a creditor has expressed an intention to release a debt relating to electronically registered stocks, etc.;
4. Where there is a merger of investment trusts under Article 193 of the Financial Investment Services and Capital Markets Act or a merger of investment companies under Article 204 of that Act;
5. Other cases prescribed and publicly notified by the Financial Services Commission where it is clear that rights to electronically registered stocks, etc. have been modified or extinguished.
(2) A person who intends to modify or cancel a new electronic registration pursuant to Article 33(1) of the Act must apply for modification or cancellation of the electronic registration to the electronic registration institution or account management institution with which the relevant electronically registered stocks, etc. are electronically registered, specifying the following matters in detail:
1. The type, issue, and quantity or amount by issue of the relevant electronically registered stocks, etc.;
2. The name of the right holder;
3. Other matters prescribed by the electronic registration business rules as necessary for electronic registration of modification or cancellation of a new electronic registration, such as matters concerning changes in the substance of rights relating to electronically registered stocks, etc.
(3) An electronic registration institution or account management institution that receives an application under paragraph (2) must electronically register the modification or cancellation of the new electronic registration in accordance with the order and methods according to the following classifications:
1. In the case of an application for modification or cancellation in respect of electronically registered stocks, etc. electronically registered in a customer account register:
(a) The account management institution must electronically register a modification or cancellation of the electronic registration of the relevant electronically registered stocks, etc. in the customer account register, and then notify the electronic registration institution of that fact without delay;
(b) The electronic registration institution must, without delay, make an entry of a modification or cancellation in the customer management account register of the relevant account management institution in accordance with the notification;
(c) The electronic registration institution must make an entry of a modification or cancellation in the issuer management account register;
2. In the case of an application for modification or cancellation in respect of electronically registered stocks, etc. electronically registered in a proprietary account register of account management institutions, etc.:
(a) The electronic registration institution must modify or cancel the electronic registration of the relevant electronically registered stocks, etc. in the proprietary account register of account management institutions, etc.;
(b) The electronic registration institution must make an entry of a modification or cancellation in the issuer management account register.

Article 29 (Electronic Registration of Modifications and Cancellations Ex Officio)
(1) "Cases prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 33(3)3 of the Act means any of the following cases:
1. Where there is a court judgment, decision, or order;
2. Where an electronic registration institution or account management institution cancels an electronic registration in order to eliminate an excess pursuant to Article 42 of the Act;
3. Other cases prescribed and publicly notified by the Financial Services Commission where it is clear that rights to electronically registered stocks, etc. have been modified or extinguished.
(2) Where an electronic registration institution or account management institution modifies or cancels the substance of rights relating to electronically registered stocks, etc. ex officio pursuant to Article 33(3) of the Act, it must follow the order and methods according to the following classifications:
1. In the case of electronically registered stocks, etc. electronically registered in a customer account register:
(a) The electronic registration institution must make an entry of a modification or cancellation in the customer management account register of the account management institution with which the relevant customer account was opened;
(b) The electronic registration institution must make an entry of a modification or cancellation in the issuer management account register, and then notify the relevant account management institution of that fact without delay;
(c) The account management institution must, without delay, modify or cancel the electronic registration of the electronically registered stocks, etc. in the relevant customer account register, and then notify the electronic registration institution of the result;
2. In the case of electronically registered stocks, etc. electronically registered in a proprietary account register of account management institutions, etc.:
(a) The electronic registration institution must modify or cancel the electronic registration of the relevant electronically registered stocks, etc. in the proprietary account register of account management institutions, etc.;
(b) The electronic registration institution must make an entry of a modification or cancellation in the issuer management account register.

Chapter V Exercise of Rights to Electronically Registered Stocks, etc.

Article 30 (Exception to Preparation of a List of Owners)
"Cases prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the proviso to Article 37(1) of the Act means cases where an investment company under the Financial Investment Services and Capital Markets Act allocates distributions arising from the settlement of the investment company's accounts.

Article 31 (Intervals and Grounds for Preparing Lists of Owners)
(1) "Interval prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 37(2)2 of the Act means a quarter (a quarterly period).
(2) "Stocks, etc. prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 37(2)3 of the Act means stocks, etc. falling under either of the following:
1. Exchangeable bonds;
2. Rights referred to in subparagraph 1(l) of Article 2 of the Act and bonds referred to in Article 469(2)3 of the Commercial Act. In such cases, this is limited to those for which the underlying assets that may be acquired through the exercise of rights are rights that may or must be represented by securities falling under any subparagraph of Article 139 of the Enforcement Decree of the Financial Investment Services and Capital Markets Act.
(3) "Persons prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 37(2)3 of the Act means the persons according to the following classifications:
1. In the case of rights represented by securities depository receipts: The issuer of the underlying stocks, etc. (limited to stocks, etc. for which the underlying assets that may be acquired through the exercise of rights attached to those stocks, etc. are rights that may or must be represented by securities falling under any subparagraph of Article 139 of the Enforcement Decree of the Financial Investment Services and Capital Markets Act; hereinafter the same shall apply in this paragraph);
2. In the case of exchangeable bonds: The issuer of the stocks, etc. subject to exchange;
3. In the case of the rights and bonds referred to in paragraph (2)2: The issuer of the stocks, etc. constituting their underlying assets.
(4) "Cases prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 37(2)4 of the Act means any of the following cases:
1. Where an administrator prepares a list of shareholders and equity holders pursuant to Article 147(1) of the Debtor Rehabilitation and Bankruptcy Act;
2. Where an issuer of stocks undergoes a listing review (meaning a review by an exchange under Article 8-2(2) of the Financial Investment Services and Capital Markets Act of securities to be listed on the securities market in accordance with the securities listing regulations under Article 390 of that Act), and designates a certain date and requests an electronic registration institution to notify it of matters regarding shareholders in order to ascertain the status of stock ownership, etc.;
3. Where an issuer must identify the owners of the relevant electronically registered stocks, etc. as prescribed in the basis for issuing stocks, etc. according to the following classifications:
(a) In the case of stocks, etc. electronically registered pursuant to Article 356-2, 420-4, 478(3), or 516-7 of the Commercial Act: The articles of incorporation of the issuer of the relevant stocks, etc.;
(b) In the case of other electronically registered stocks, etc.: A contract, terms and conditions, or an equivalent instrument relating to the issuance of the relevant stocks, etc. that constitutes the basis for issuing the stocks, etc.;
4. Other cases prescribed and publicly notified by the Financial Services Commission where special circumstances, such as a need to protect the interests of right holders, have arisen and it is necessary to identify the owners of the relevant electronically registered stocks, etc.
(5) "Cases prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 37(3) of the Act means any of the following cases: <Amended on June 27, 2023>
1. Where redeemable bonds under Article 469(2)2 of the Commercial Act are redeemed with other stocks, etc.;
2. Where rights required to be represented by contingent capital securities under the Banking Act, the Financial Holding Companies Act, and the Insurance Business Act are converted into stocks;
3. Other cases prescribed and publicly notified by the Financial Services Commission where stocks, etc. in bearer form that are electronically registered stocks, etc. are converted into other stocks, etc.
(6) "Grounds prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 37(7)3 of the Act means any of the following cases:
1. Where there is a court judgment, decision, or order;
2. Where an electronic registration institution or account management institution cancels an electronic registration in order to eliminate an excess pursuant to Article 42 of the Act;
3. Other cases prescribed by the electronic registration business rules where it is recognized that it is difficult for an electronic registration institution to manage rights relating to stocks, etc.

Article 32 (Exercise of Rights through an Electronic Registration Institution)
(1) "Matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 38(3) of the Act means the following matters:
1. The type and issuance number (sequence number) of the electronically registered stocks, etc.;
2. The types of rights to the electronically registered stocks, etc., the grounds for their accrual, their substance, and the schedule for exercising the rights;
3. Where the terms of issuance of the electronically registered stocks, etc. have been changed, the details of the changes;
4. Other matters prescribed by the electronic registration business rules in relation to the exercise of rights to electronically registered stocks, etc.
(2) Where a ground for conversion into stocks or debt restructuring arises in respect of contingent capital securities, the issuer of the contingent capital securities under Article 165-11(1) of the Financial Investment Services and Capital Markets Act must notify the electronic registration institution of that fact without delay pursuant to Article 38(3) of the Act so that the right holders of the relevant contingent capital securities may exercise their rights through the electronic registration institution pursuant to paragraph (1) of that Article.
(3) Where the ground notified pursuant to paragraph (2) is the occurrence of a ground for conversion into stocks, the electronic registration institution must, without delay, notify the issuer or transfer agent company of the following matters regarding owners as of the second business day from the date on which the ground for conversion into stocks arose:
1. The names and addresses of owners of the contingent capital securities;
2. The amount of contingent capital securities held by each owner.

Article 33 (Methods for Issuing Ownership Certificates, etc.)
(1) Where an electronic registration institution receives an application from an owner of electronically registered stocks, etc. for the issuance of a document certifying electronic registration of the electronically registered stocks, etc. (hereinafter referred to as an "ownership certificate") pursuant to Article 39 (1) of the Act, or receives notice from an account management institution pursuant to paragraph (2) of that Article, it shall issue an ownership certificate prepared as follows according to the institution with which the stocks, etc. are electronically registered:
1. Ownership certificate for stocks, etc. electronically registered with an electronic registration institution: The particulars to be certified shall be prepared based on the proprietary register of account management institutions, etc.;
2. Ownership certificate for stocks, etc. electronically registered with an account management institution: The particulars to be certified shall be prepared based on the customer register notified to the electronic registration institution by the relevant account management institution.
(2) An electronic registration institution shall enter the following matters in an ownership certificate:
1. The name and address of the owner of the electronically registered stocks, etc.;
2. The type, issue, and quantity or amount of the electronically registered stocks, etc.;
3. The details of the rights that the owner of the electronically registered stocks, etc. intends to exercise;
4. The recipient to whom the ownership certificate is to be submitted;
5. Other matters prescribed by the electronic registration business rules relating to proof of status as an owner of electronically registered stocks, etc.
(3) "Matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 39 (2) of the Act means the matters specified in paragraph (2) 1, 4, and 5.
(4) "A person prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 39 (3) of the Act means the relevant court where an owner intends to make an application or claim to a court or file a lawsuit to exercise rights to electronically registered stocks, etc.
(5) Where an electronic registration institution or account management institution makes an electronic registration in the electronic registration account register restricting disposition of the electronically registered stocks, etc. on which the issuance of an ownership certificate is based pursuant to Article 39 (4) of the Act, it shall indicate that the issuance of the ownership certificate is the cause of that electronic registration.
(6) "Persons prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 39 (5) of the Act means any of the following persons:
1. A court under paragraph (4);
2. A bond management company under the Commercial Act;
3. Other persons who need to exercise rights as owners of electronically registered stocks, etc. on the basis of ownership certificates and who are determined and publicly notified by the Financial Services Commission.

Article 34 (Methods for Giving Notice of Ownership Details, etc.)
(1) Where an electronic registration institution receives an application from an owner of electronically registered stocks, etc. to notify the issuer of the details of ownership of the electronically registered stocks, etc. pursuant to Article 40 (1) of the Act, or receives notice from an account management institution pursuant to paragraph (2) of that Article, it shall give notice of ownership details prepared as follows according to the institution with which the stocks, etc. are electronically registered:
1. Ownership details of stocks, etc. electronically registered with an electronic registration institution: The details shall be prepared based on the proprietary register of account management institutions, etc.;
2. Ownership details of stocks, etc. electronically registered with an account management institution: The details shall be prepared based on the customer register notified to the electronic registration institution by the relevant account management institution.
(2) Where an electronic registration institution gives notice of ownership details of electronically registered stocks, etc. pursuant to paragraph (1), it shall include the following matters:
1. The name and address of the owner of the electronically registered stocks, etc.;
2. The type, issue, and quantity or amount of the electronically registered stocks, etc.;
3. The details of the rights that the owner of the electronically registered stocks, etc. intends to exercise;
4. The period of validity of the notified details;
5. Other matters prescribed by the electronic registration business rules relating to notice of ownership details of electronically registered stocks, etc.
(3) Where an electronic registration institution gives notice to issuers, etc. of ownership details of electronically registered stocks, etc. pursuant to Article 40 (1) of the Act, it shall do so by any of the following methods:
1. In writing or by fax;
2. By email or other similar electronic communications;
3. Other methods prescribed by public notice of the Financial Services Commission.
(4) "Matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 40 (2) of the Act means the matters specified in paragraph (2) 1, 4, and 5.
(5) Where an electronic registration institution or account management institution makes an electronic registration restricting disposition of the electronically registered stocks, etc. on which notice of ownership details is based pursuant to Article 40 (3) of the Act, it shall, without delay, indicate in the proprietary register of account management institutions, etc. or the customer register the period during which disposition of those electronically registered stocks, etc. is restricted and that the cause of the restriction is the notice of ownership details.

CHAPTER VI ENSURING THE SAFETY OF ELECTRONIC REGISTRATION

Article 35 (Methods for Eliminating Excess Quantities or Amounts, etc.)
(1) Where an excess quantity or amount under Article 42 (1) of the Act arises, an account management institution shall check the customer accounts and, without delay, make an electronic registration to cancel the excess quantity or amount.
(2) Where an excess quantity or amount under Article 42 (2) of the Act arises, an electronic registration institution shall check the proprietary accounts of account management institutions, etc. or the customer management accounts under Article 22 (3) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "customer management accounts") and, without delay, make an electronic registration to cancel the excess quantity or amount.
(3) Where there is a person who has lawfully acquired rights to an excess quantity or amount under Article 42 (1) or (2) of the Act pursuant to Article 35 (5) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as a "good-faith acquirer of an excess quantity or amount"), the account management institution or electronic registration institution shall, without delay, make an electronic registration to cancel a quantity or amount of the electronically registered stocks, etc. in which the excess arose (hereinafter referred to as an "issue subject to excess electronic registration") equivalent to the excess quantity or amount acquired in good faith by that person. In such cases, an account management institution or electronic registration institution that does not hold the issue subject to excess electronic registration shall acquire it and make an electronic registration to cancel it.
(4) Where an account management institution or electronic registration institution fails to perform all or part of its obligation to eliminate an excess quantity or amount under paragraph (3), the excess quantity or amount shall be eliminated in the following order and manner:
1. It shall be eliminated using funds set aside by the electronic registration institution to ensure the safety of electronic registration (meaning funds set aside by reflecting them in the business plan under Article 3 (3) 4 in accordance with methods jointly determined and publicly notified by the Financial Services Commission and the Minister of Justice);
2. Where the excess quantity or amount is not fully eliminated by the method under subparagraph 1, it shall be eliminated using contributions from all account management institutions determined by methods jointly determined and publicly notified by the Financial Services Commission and the Minister of Justice, taking into account the final market price on the date the excess quantity or amount arose and the volume of electronically registered stocks, etc. In such cases, the electronic registration institution shall bear the contribution of an account management institution that lacks the ability to bear it.
(5) An account management institution or electronic registration institution that has eliminated an excess quantity or amount pursuant to paragraph (4) may exercise a right of recourse against the person responsible for the occurrence of the excess quantity or amount pursuant to Article 42 (5) of the Act.
(6) Where, despite the exercise of the right of recourse under paragraph (5), any amount of the funds used by the electronic registration institution to eliminate the excess quantity or amount has not been recovered, all account management institutions shall bear that amount in proportion to the contributions determined by the calculation method under paragraph (4) 2.
(7) "The amount prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 42 (4) of the Act means all money, including distributions, that the issuer must pay to persons electronically registered as right holders of the electronically registered stocks, etc. in which the excess quantity or amount has arisen.
(8) An account management institution or electronic registration institution that has failed to perform its obligation to eliminate an excess quantity or amount shall be obligated to pay the amount under Article 42 (4) of the Act according to the following categories:
1. Account management institution: An obligation to pay principal, interest, etc. corresponding to the quantity or amount calculated pursuant to Article 36 (2) to persons who are electronically registered as right holders of the relevant electronically registered stocks, etc. in the customer register of the account management institution whose obligation to eliminate the excess quantity or amount has arisen pursuant to Article 42 (1) of the Act and who fall under Article 36 (1) 2;
2. Electronic registration institution: Where an obligation to eliminate an excess quantity or amount has arisen pursuant to Article 42 (2) of the Act, an obligation to pay principal, interest, etc. corresponding to the quantity or amount calculated pursuant to Article 36 (4) to persons who are electronically registered as right holders of the relevant electronically registered stocks, etc. and who fall under Article 36 (3) 2.
(9) Matters necessary for eliminating excess quantities or amounts and other related matters, other than those prescribed in paragraphs (3) through (8), shall be determined and publicly notified by the Financial Services Commission.

Article 36 (Restrictions on the Exercise of Rights to Excess Quantities or Amounts)
(1) "Persons prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 43 (1) of the Act means persons falling under either of the following categories:
1. Where there is no good-faith acquirer of an excess quantity or amount: Persons electronically registered as right holders of the excess quantity or amount;
2. Where there is a good-faith acquirer of an excess quantity or amount: Persons electronically registered as right holders of the issue subject to excess electronic registration.
(2) The quantity or amount for which a person under paragraph (1) may not assert rights against the issuer pursuant to Article 43 (1) of the Act shall be the quantity or amount calculated according to the following categories:
1. Where there is no good-faith acquirer of an excess quantity or amount: The quantity or amount, out of the excess quantity or amount under Article 42 (1) of the Act, electronically registered in the customer register of each person electronically registered as a right holder;
2. Where there is a good-faith acquirer of an excess quantity or amount: The quantity or amount calculated by the following formula:

[Quantity or amount, out of the excess quantity or amount under Article 42 (1) of the Act, acquired in good faith pursuant to Article 35 (5) of the Act] × [Quantity or amount of the issue subject to excess electronic registration electronically registered in each right holder's customer register] ÷ [Total quantity or amount of the issue subject to excess electronic registration electronically registered in all customer registers of the relevant account management institution]

(3) "Persons prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 43 (2) of the Act means persons falling under either of the following categories:
1. Where there is no good-faith acquirer of an excess quantity or amount: Persons electronically registered as right holders of the excess quantity or amount;
2. Where there is a good-faith acquirer of an excess quantity or amount: Persons electronically registered as right holders of the issue subject to excess electronic registration.
(4) The quantity or amount for which a person under paragraph (3) may not assert rights against the issuer pursuant to Article 43 (2) of the Act shall be the quantity or amount calculated according to the following categories:
1. Where there is no good-faith acquirer of an excess quantity or amount: The quantity or amount, out of the excess quantity or amount under Article 42 (2) of the Act, electronically registered in the proprietary register of account management institutions, etc. of each person electronically registered as a right holder;
2. Where there is a good-faith acquirer of an excess quantity or amount: The quantity or amount calculated by the following formula:

[Quantity or amount, out of the excess quantity or amount under Article 42 (2) of the Act, acquired in good faith pursuant to Article 35 (5) of the Act] × [Quantity or amount of the issue subject to excess electronic registration electronically registered in each right holder's proprietary register of account management institutions, etc. or customer register] ÷ [Total quantity or amount of the issue subject to excess electronic registration electronically registered in all proprietary registers of account management institutions, etc. and customer registers]

Article 37 (Matters to Be Reported by Electronic Registration Institutions)
"Grounds prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 46 (3) 3 of the Act means grounds determined and publicly notified by the Financial Services Commission as making it impossible to normally perform affairs for the electronic registration, recording, and management of electronically registered stocks, etc. due to a natural disaster, computer system failure, or other comparable situation.

Article 38 (Restrictions on Electronic Registration of Transfers between Accounts)
(1) "Grounds prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 47 of the Act means any of the following grounds:
1. Revocation of an account management institution's authorization, permission, registration, or other approval, or suspension of its business;
2. Bankruptcy or dissolution of an account management institution, or other grounds equivalent to those specified in subparagraph 1 that are determined and publicly notified by the Financial Services Commission as making it impossible to normally perform affairs for the electronic registration of transfers between accounts.
(2) Where an electronic registration institution restricts electronic registration of transfers between accounts of electronically registered stocks, etc. electronically registered in customer registers pursuant to Article 47 of the Act, it may impose restrictions by type or issue of the relevant electronically registered stocks, etc.
(3) Where an electronic registration institution restricts electronic registration of transfers between accounts of electronically registered stocks, etc. pursuant to paragraph (2), it shall publicly announce the details on its website.

Article 39 (Retention of Electronic Registration Information, etc.)
(1) The electronic registration information or recorded information that electronic registration institutions and account management institutions must retain pursuant to Article 48 (1) of the Act shall be as follows:
1. Information to be retained by an electronic registration institution: The information specified in the following items:
(a) Information electronically registered in the proprietary register of account management institutions, etc.;
(b) Information recorded in the issuer management register and customer management register.
2. Information to be retained by an account management institution: Information electronically registered in the customer register.
(2) An electronic registration institution or account management institution shall retain electronic registration information or recorded information under paragraph (1) by methods satisfying all of the following requirements:
1. The information shall be retained using a device that makes forgery or alteration impossible;
2. The same information shall be retained at two or more locations. In such cases, retention at one location may be entrusted to a person who manages that location and possesses sufficient personnel, computer facilities, security facilities, and other physical facilities necessary for information protection.
(3) The retention periods for information under paragraph (1) shall be as follows:
1. Information specified in the items of paragraph (1) 1: Permanently;
2. Information under paragraph (1) 2: Ten years from the date on which the relevant customer register is closed.

CHAPTER VII INSPECTION AND SUPERVISION

Article 40 (Measures against Electronic Registration Institutions)
(1) "Cases prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 53 (1) 6 of the Act means any of the following cases:
1. Failure to obtain approval in violation of the former part of Article 15 (1), the former part of Article 16, or the former part of Article 17 of the Act;
2. Failure to implement measures under Article 49 (1) of the Act.
(2) "Financial statutes and regulations, etc. prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 53 (1) 7 of the Act means the following statutes:
1. The Act on Real Name Financial Transactions and Confidentiality;
2. The Criminal Act;
3. The Act on the Aggravated Punishment, etc. of Specific Economic Crimes.
(3) "Cases prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 53 (1) 7 of the Act means any of the following cases:
1. A violation of the Act on Real Name Financial Transactions and Confidentiality falling under any of the following items:
(a) Providing or disclosing to another person information or materials concerning the details of financial transactions (hereinafter referred to as "transaction information, etc." in this subparagraph), or requesting the provision thereof, in violation of the main clause of Article 4 (1) of the Act on Real Name Financial Transactions and Confidentiality;
(b) Failing to refuse a request for the provision of transaction information, etc. in violation of Article 4 (3) of the Act on Real Name Financial Transactions and Confidentiality;
(c) Providing or disclosing to another person transaction information, etc. that has become known, using it for a purpose other than its intended purpose, or requesting its provision, in violation of the main clause of Article 4 (4) of the Act on Real Name Financial Transactions and Confidentiality;
(d) Providing or disclosing to another person transaction information, etc. that has been obtained, in violation of Article 4 (5) of the Act on Real Name Financial Transactions and Confidentiality.
2. Committing an offense under Articles 214 through 217, Article 223 (limited to attempts to commit offenses under Articles 214 through 217), Article 347-2, Article 355, Article 356, Article 357 (1), or Article 359 (limited to attempts to commit offenses under Articles 355 and 356 and Article 357 (1)) of the Criminal Act;
3. Committing an offense under Article 3 (limited to cases where an offense under Article 355 or 356 of the Criminal Act is committed), Articles 5, 7, and 8, or Article 9 (3) of the Act on the Aggravated Punishment, etc. of Specific Economic Crimes.
(4) "Cases prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 53 (1) 11 of the Act means any of the following cases:
1. Failing to commence business within six months from the date permission for electronic registration business was granted (meaning the separately specified deadline where a deadline has been specified pursuant to Article 5 (10)), or discontinuing the permitted business without justifiable grounds after commencing business;
2. Failing to remedy the matter that caused a measure suspending all or part of the business within one month from the date on which the measure under Article 53 (3) 1 of the Act was imposed (or the specified remedial period where a remedial period exceeding one month was specified when imposing the suspension);
3. Improperly receiving money or other property from another person, or acquiring money or other property to be given to another person, in connection with business;
4. Continuing or repeating the same or similar unlawful acts.
(5) "Measures prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 53 (3) 7 of the Act means any of the following measures:
1. A demand or recommendation to improve management or business methods;
2. A demand for compensation;
3. Where the Act has been violated, filing an accusation or notifying an investigative agency;
4. Where another Act has been violated, notifying a relevant institution or investigative agency;
5. Other measures that the Financial Services Commission may take under the Act, this Decree, or other relevant statutes and regulations.
(6) "Measures prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 53 (4) 6 of the Act means the measures under paragraph (5) 3 and 4.
(7) "Measures prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 53 (5) 7 of the Act means the measures under paragraph (5) 3 and 4.
(8) "Cases prescribed by Presidential Decree" in subparagraph 45 of attached Table 1 of the Act means any of the following cases:
1. Issuing an ownership certificate in violation of Article 33;
2. Giving notice of ownership details in violation of Article 34;
3. Issuing an electronic registration certificate in violation of Article 44;
4. Violating the electronic registration business rules;
5. Violating rules governing business other than the electronic registration business rules under the main clause of Article 18 of the Act.

Article 41 (Transfer of Electronic Registration Information, etc.)
Where an electronic registration institution receives an order to transfer its business pursuant to Article 57 (1) of the Act, it shall transfer the information specified in the items of Article 39 (1) 1 to another electronic registration institution in accordance with that business transfer order.

Article 42 (Account Management Institutions Excluded from Inspection)
"Institutions prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the former part of Article 58 (1) of the Act means the following institutions:
1. Foreign electronic registration institutions under Article 19, subparagraph 5 of the Act;
2. Resolution finance companies under Article 36-3 (1) of the Depositor Protection Act;
3. Where compensation bonds under Article 72 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act are held with a project implementer serving as the account management institution pursuant to paragraph (3) of that Article, the relevant project implementer;
4. Other institutions determined and publicly notified by the Financial Services Commission in consideration of the nature of their business, the necessity of inspection, and other relevant matters.

CHAPTER VIII SUPPLEMENTARY PROVISIONS

Article 43 (Disclosure of Issuance Details)
(1) "Issuance details prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 62 (1) of the Act means the following matters:
1. The issuance round and aggregate issue price of electronically registered stocks, etc.;
2. In the case of short-term bonds, etc., the issuance limit and the outstanding amount issued;
3. Other matters prescribed by the electronic registration business rules relating to issuance details of electronically registered stocks, etc.
(2) An electronic registration institution separately designated by the Financial Services Commission pursuant to Article 62 (2) of the Act shall establish a separate website for the disclosure of issuance details and shall use it to disclose together the issuance details of stocks, etc. electronically registered with that electronic registration institution and the issuance details notified by other electronic registration institutions.

Article 44 (Electronic Registration Certificates)
(1) Where an electronic registration institution issues an electronic registration certificate under Article 63 (1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as an "electronic registration certificate" in this Article), it shall issue the certificate according to the following categories:
1. Stocks, etc. electronically registered in a customer register: Issuance based on the customer register notified to the electronic registration institution by the relevant account management institution;
2. Stocks, etc. electronically registered in the proprietary register of account management institutions, etc.: Issuance based on the proprietary register of account management institutions, etc.
(2) An electronic registration certificate shall state the following matters:
1. The name and address of the owner as entered in the customer register or proprietary register of account management institutions, etc.;
2. The type and quantity or amount of the electronically registered stocks, etc.;
3. The purpose for which the electronic registration certificate is to be used;
4. A statement that the electronic registration certificate may be used only to make a deposit under the Deposit Act or to make payment in lieu of a security deposit or deposited money pursuant to Article 171 of the Financial Investment Services and Capital Markets Act;
5. A statement that a person entitled to receive electronically registered stocks, etc. deposited under the Deposit Act, or the State, a local government, or a public institution under the Act on the Management of Public Institutions (hereinafter referred to as a "public institution" in this paragraph) that has received electronically registered stocks, etc. in lieu of a security deposit or deposited money pursuant to Article 171 of the Financial Investment Services and Capital Markets Act, may apply for electronic registration of a transfer between accounts of the relevant electronically registered stocks, etc. to its own electronic registration account;
6. A statement that, where a person entitled to receive electronically registered stocks, etc. deposited under the Deposit Act, the State, a local government, or a public institution applies for electronic registration of a transfer between accounts pursuant to subparagraph 5, it must return the relevant electronic registration certificate to the electronic registration institution or account management institution, and that, in such cases, the electronic registration institution or account management institution cancels the electronic registration restricting disposition pursuant to Article 63 (2) of the Act;
7. A statement that an account management institution to which an electronic registration certificate has been returned must return it to the electronic registration institution without delay.
(3) A person intending to subject electronically registered stocks, etc. whose disposition is restricted pursuant to Article 63 (3) of the Act to attachment (including provisional attachment; hereinafter the same shall apply in this paragraph) shall apply to a court for attachment of the rights specified in the following subparagraphs:
1. Where an electronic registration certificate has been issued to make a deposit under the Deposit Act: The right to claim withdrawal or recovery of the deposited property;
2. Where an electronic registration certificate has been issued to provide electronically registered stocks, etc. in lieu of a security deposit or deposited money pursuant to Article 171 of the Financial Investment Services and Capital Markets Act: The right to claim return of the electronic registration certificate.

Article 45 (Entrustment of Authority)
Pursuant to Article 69 of the Act, the Financial Services Commission shall entrust the following authority to the Governor of the Financial Supervisory Service: Provided, That affairs determined and publicly notified by the Financial Services Commission as requiring expedited handling or other measures to protect right holders and maintain sound trading practices shall be excluded.
1. Measures under Article 53 (3) 5 and 6 of the Act;
2. Measures under Article 53 (4) 4 and 5 of the Act;
3. Requests for measures under Article 53 (5) 2 through 6 of the Act;
4. Measures and requests for measures under the main clause of Article 53 (6) of the Act (limited to measures under paragraph (4) 4 and 5 of that Article and requests for measures under paragraph (5) 2 through 6 of that Article);
5. Recording, maintenance, and management of the details of dispositions and measures under Article 55 (1) of the Act; notification concerning officers and employees who have left office or retired under the former part of paragraph (3) of that Article; receipt of requests for inquiries under paragraph (5) of that Article; and notification under paragraph (6) of that Article.

Article 46 (Processing of Personally Identifiable Information)
(1) "Affairs prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 70 of the Act means any of the following affairs:
1. Affairs concerning verification of details of financial investment product transactions by officers and employees of electronic registration institutions under Article 63 (3) of the Financial Investment Services and Capital Markets Act, which applies mutatis mutandis pursuant to Article 13 (6) of the Act;
2. Affairs concerning transfer agency services for stocks, etc. under Article 14 (3) 1 (a) of the Act;
3. Affairs concerning the opening of issuer management accounts under Article 21 of the Act;
4. Affairs concerning the opening of proprietary accounts of account management institutions, etc. under Article 23 of the Act;
5. Affairs concerning preparation of the list of owners under Article 37 of the Act;
6. Affairs concerning the exercise of rights to electronically registered stocks, etc. under Article 38 of the Act;
7. Affairs concerning the issuance of ownership certificates under Article 39 of the Act;
8. Affairs concerning notice of ownership details under Article 40 of the Act;
9. Affairs concerning the issuance of electronic registration certificates under Article 63 (1) of the Act.
(2) "Information prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 70 of the Act means resident registration numbers, passport numbers, driver's license numbers, and alien registration numbers under Article 19 of the Enforcement Decree of the Personal Information Protection Act.

Article 47 (Change of Electronic Registration Institution)
(1) "Matters prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as the details of rights to stocks, etc. electronically registered by the relevant issuer" in Article 71 (1) of the Act means the following matters:
1. Matters recorded in the issuer management register, such as the details of rights to stocks, etc. electronically registered by the relevant issuer;
2. Matters recorded in the customer management register, such as the details of rights to stocks, etc. electronically registered by the relevant issuer;
3. Matters electronically registered in the proprietary register of account management institutions, etc., such as the details of rights to stocks, etc. electronically registered by the relevant issuer.
(2) An electronic registration institution that has notified an issuer pursuant to Article 71 (1) of the Act shall, without delay, record cancellation of the details of rights to stocks, etc. electronically registered by the relevant issuer and other relevant matters in the issuer management register, and make an electronic registration of cancellation in the proprietary register of account management institutions, etc.
(3) An electronic registration institution that has received notice from an issuer pursuant to Article 71 (2) of the Act shall take measures according to the following categories:
1. Where the notified details include matters to be recorded with an electronic registration institution: Record them in the issuer management register;
2. Where the notified details include matters to be electronically registered with an electronic registration institution: Electronically register them in the proprietary register of account management institutions, etc.;
3. Where the notified details include matters to be electronically registered with an account management institution: Record them in the customer management register and, without delay, notify the account management institution with which each right holder concerned with the notified details has opened a customer account.
(4) Matters necessary concerning the methods and procedures for notice resulting from a change of electronic registration institution and other matters, other than those prescribed in paragraphs (2) and (3), shall be determined and publicly notified by the Financial Services Commission.

Article 48 (Prior Consultation with the Minister of Justice)
Where the Financial Services Commission intends to establish or amend a public notice pursuant to this Decree, it shall consult with the Minister of Justice in advance.

CHAPTER IX PENALTY PROVISIONS

Article 49 (Criteria for Imposing Administrative Fines)
The criteria for imposing administrative fines under Article 75 (1) and (2) of the Act shall be as specified in attached Table 3.

ADDENDA <Presidential Decree No. 29892, June 25, 2019>

Article 1 (Enforcement Date)
This Decree shall enter into force on September 16, 2019: Provided, That Articles 2, 4, 5, and 8 of the Addenda shall enter into force on the date of promulgation.

Article 2 (Provisions on Enforcement of the Act on Electronic Registration of Stocks, Bonds, etc.)
The Act on Electronic Registration of Stocks, Bonds, etc., Act No. 14096, shall enter into force on September 16, 2019: Provided, That Article 3 (3) through (9), Article 4 (1), (3), and (4), and Article 8 (1) and (2) of the Addenda to the Act shall enter into force on the date of promulgation of this Decree.
[Enforcement date: June 25, 2019] Article 2

Article 3 (Repeal of Other Statutes)
Each of the following statutes is repealed:
1. Enforcement Decree of the Public and Corporate Bond Registration Act;
2. Enforcement Decree of the Act on the Issuance and Distribution of Electronic Short-Term Bonds, etc.

Article 4 (Special Cases concerning Conversion into Electronically Registered Stocks, etc.)
(1) With respect to stocks, etc. converted into electronically registered stocks, etc. pursuant to Article 3 (1) of the Addenda to the Act as at the time this Decree enters into force, among accounts opened by depositors under Article 309 (1) of the Financial Investment Services and Capital Markets Act, accounts for holdings owned by the depositors themselves and accounts for holdings deposited by investors shall be deemed converted into proprietary accounts of account management institutions, etc. and customer management accounts, respectively. Accounts opened by depositors under Article 310 (1) of the Financial Investment Services and Capital Markets Act to manage securities, etc. deposited by investors shall be deemed converted into customer accounts.
(2) With respect to stocks, etc. converted into electronically registered stocks, etc. pursuant to Article 3 (1) of the Addenda to the Act as at the time this Decree enters into force, the portions for holdings owned by depositors themselves and for holdings deposited by investors in the depositor account register under Article 309 (3) of the Financial Investment Services and Capital Markets Act shall be deemed converted into the proprietary account register of account management institutions, etc. and the customer management account register, respectively. The investor account register under Article 310 (1) of the Financial Investment Services and Capital Markets Act shall be deemed converted into the customer account register.
(3) Where stocks, etc. are converted into electronically registered stocks, etc. pursuant to Article 3 (1) of the Addenda to the Act, the electronic registration institution shall open issuer management accounts pursuant to Article 21 (1) of the Act and prepare an issuer management account register for each issuer pursuant to paragraph (2) of that Article.
(4) An owner who intends, pursuant to the latter part of Article 3 (2) of the Addenda to the Act, to convert into electronically registered stocks, etc. public and corporate bonds registered with the Korea Securities Depository under the former Public and Corporate Bond Registration Act (meaning that Act before its repeal by Act No. 14096; hereinafter the same shall apply) but not deposited with the Korea Securities Depository as at September 16, 2019 (hereinafter in this Article referred to as "undeposited registered public and corporate bonds") shall apply to the Korea Securities Depository for conversion into electronically registered stocks, etc.
(5) Upon receiving an application under paragraph (4), the Korea Securities Depository shall notify the issuer of the undeposited registered public and corporate bonds that their owner has applied for conversion into electronically registered stocks, etc., and shall notify the electronic registration institution of the particulars of the conversion application in accordance with the intent of the owner's application.
(6) Upon receiving notice under paragraph (5), the electronic registration institution shall carry out electronic registration in accordance with the particulars of the conversion application and notify the Korea Securities Depository thereof without delay.
(7) Upon receiving notice under paragraph (6), the Korea Securities Depository shall cancel the registration of the relevant undeposited registered public and corporate bonds in the public and corporate bond register under Article 9 of the former Public and Corporate Bond Registration Act.
(8) Matters necessary for the method and procedure for converting undeposited registered public and corporate bonds into electronically registered stocks, etc., and other matters relating to conversion, other than those prescribed in paragraphs (4) through (7), shall be prescribed by the electronic registration business rules.
(9) Article 22 (2) and (3) shall apply mutatis mutandis to the methods of public announcement and notification where an issuer makes public announcements and notifications pursuant to Article 3 (3) of the Addenda to the Act.
(10) Where an issuer, pursuant to Article 3 (3) of the Addenda to the Act, notifies persons entered in the register of shareholders, etc. as right holders of stock certificates, etc. subject to conversion (meaning stock certificates, etc. representing rights in stocks, etc. converted into electronically registered stocks, etc. pursuant to Article 3 (1) of the Addenda to the Act; hereinafter the same shall apply), the persons to be notified shall be determined on the basis of the right holders entered in the register of shareholders, etc. as at June 30, 2019.
(11) Where, as at the time this Decree enters into force, a right holder of undeposited stock certificates, etc. subject to conversion fails to give notice of an electronic registration account or submit the stock certificates, etc. subject to conversion pursuant to Article 3 (3) 2 of the Addenda to the Act, transfer agent companies, etc. under Article 29 (1) of the Act shall, on behalf of the issuer pursuant to paragraph (4) of that Article, open a special account for the right holder and prepare a special account register under paragraph (2) of that Article for each issuer.
(12) In the case of stocks, etc. converted into electronically registered stocks, etc. pursuant to Article 3 (1) of the Addenda to the Act which are public and corporate bonds registered with the Korea Securities Depository under the former Public and Corporate Bond Registration Act, the Korea Securities Depository shall cancel their registration in the public and corporate bond register under Article 9 of that Act.
(13) Detailed matters necessary for converting stocks, etc. (excluding undeposited registered public and corporate bonds) into electronically registered stocks, etc. pursuant to Article 3 (1) of the Addenda to the Act, other than those prescribed in paragraphs (1) through (3) and (9) through (11), shall be prescribed and publicly notified by the Financial Services Commission.
[Enforcement date: June 25, 2019] Article 4

Article 5 (Special Cases concerning Conversion into Electronically Registered Stocks, etc. upon Application)
(1) "Last day of the period prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the provisions other than the subparagraphs of Article 4 (1) of the Addenda to the Act means the last day of the month in which the date falling two years and nine months after the date of promulgation of the Act occurs.
(2) "Matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 4 (1) 3 of the Addenda to the Act means a statement to the effect that, if an issuer does not apply pursuant to Article 4 (1) 2 of the Addenda to the Act, the issuer may apply for electronic registration pursuant to the main clause of the provisions other than the subparagraphs of Article 25 (1) of the Act after September 16, 2019.
(3) Article 4 (1), (2), (9), (10), and (11) of the Addenda to this Decree shall apply mutatis mutandis to stock certificates, etc. (meaning stock certificates, etc. under Article 21 (1) 1 of the Act) representing rights in deposited unlisted stocks, etc. converted pursuant to Article 4 (1) and (2) of the Addenda to the Act.
(4) Matters necessary for conversion into electronically registered stocks, etc. upon application, other than those prescribed in paragraphs (1) through (3), shall be prescribed and publicly notified by the Financial Services Commission.
[Enforcement date: June 25, 2019] Article 5

Article 6 (Special Cases concerning Applications for Electronic Registration of Newly Issued Stocks, etc.)
Where an issuer of stocks, etc. falling under any subparagraph of Article 25 (1) of the Act submits, together with an application for electronic registration submitted to an electronic registration institution under the former part of paragraph (3) of that Article after this Decree enters into force, both the articles of incorporation, contract, terms and conditions, or anything equivalent thereto concerning the issuance of the stocks, etc. as at the time the application is submitted (hereinafter in this Article referred to as "articles of incorporation, etc.") and proposed amendments to the articles of incorporation, etc. concerning electronic registration of the stocks, etc., the issuer shall be deemed to have submitted the documents under Article 19 (2) 1.

Article 7 (General Transitional Measures)
(1) Applications, notifications, and other acts made to an administrative agency or the Korea Securities Depository under the former Enforcement Decree of the Public and Corporate Bond Registration Act and the former Enforcement Decree of the Act on the Issuance and Distribution of Electronic Short-Term Bonds, etc. as at the time this Decree enters into force shall be deemed made under the corresponding provisions of this Decree.
(2) Registrations and other acts performed by an administrative agency or the Korea Securities Depository under the former Enforcement Decree of the Public and Corporate Bond Registration Act and the former Enforcement Decree of the Act on the Issuance and Distribution of Electronic Short-Term Bonds, etc. as at the time this Decree enters into force shall be deemed performed under the corresponding provisions of this Decree.

Article 8 (Transitional Measures concerning Korea Securities Depository)
(1) Pursuant to Article 8 (1) of the Addenda to the Act, the Korea Securities Depository shall be deemed licensed to engage in electronic registration business for licensed business unit 1 under Article 3 (1) of and Attached Table 1 to this Decree.
(2) The Korea Securities Depository deemed licensed to engage in electronic registration business pursuant to Article 8 (1) of the Addenda to the Act shall establish the financial resources necessary to ensure the stability of electronic registration under Article 35 (4) 1, as jointly prescribed and publicly notified by the Financial Services Commission and the Minister of Justice.
