(13) The Enforcement Decree of the Banking Act is partially amended as follows:
Articles 19-3 through 19-10 shall each be newly inserted as follows:

    Article 19-3 (Scope of Bonds, etc.)
    "Rights prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 33-5 (1) of the Act means the following rights:
    1. Rights that may or shall be represented by small and medium enterprise financing bonds under Article 36-2 of the Industrial Bank of Korea Act;
    2. Rights that may or shall be represented by industrial finance bonds under Article 23 of the Korea Development Bank Act;
    3. Rights that may or shall be represented by negotiable certificates of deposit.

    Article 19-4 (Applications for Registration of Bonds, etc.)
    (1) Where an owner, pledgee, or other interested party of bonds, etc. under Article 33-5 (1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "bonds, etc.") intends to register a right, the person shall submit to the bank issuing the relevant bonds, etc. (hereinafter referred to as the "issuing bank") an application for registration stating the amount and bond number of each bond, etc. to be registered and other matters necessary for registration.
    (2) Where the cause of registration under Article 33-5 (1) of the Act is an act involving a counterparty, such as a transfer or creation of a pledge, the person acquiring a right through registration (including an agent; hereinafter referred to as the "registration right holder") and the counterparty (including an agent; hereinafter referred to as the "registration obligor") shall jointly apply for registration: Provided, That the registration right holder may apply for registration alone if a written consent of the registration obligor is attached to the application for registration.
    (3) Matters necessary for applications for registration, including the applications under paragraphs (1) and (2), registration methods and procedures, and documents to be submitted, shall be prescribed and publicly notified by the Financial Services Commission.

    Article 19-5 (Issuance of Registration Certificates)
    Upon completing registration of bonds, etc., the issuing bank shall issue a registration certificate as prescribed and publicly notified by the Financial Services Commission.

    Article 19-6 (Applications for Cancellation of Registration of Bonds, etc.)
    (1) A person intending to apply for cancellation of registration of registered bonds, etc. shall submit an application for cancellation stating the amount and bond number of each bond, etc. whose registration is to be canceled and other necessary matters, together with the registration certificate under Article 19-5.
    (2) Matters necessary for applications for cancellation of registration, including the application under paragraph (1), methods and procedures for cancellation of registration, and documents to be submitted, shall be prescribed and publicly notified by the Financial Services Commission.

    Article 19-7 (Cancellation of Registration Where Whereabouts of Registration Obligor Are Unknown)
    (1) Where a registration right holder cannot apply for cancellation of registration because the whereabouts of the registration obligor are unknown, the registration right holder may apply for a public summons under the Civil Procedure Act.
    (2) Where a registration right holder cannot apply for cancellation of registration because the whereabouts of the registration obligor are unknown, and a judgment of nullification has been rendered, the registration right holder may apply alone for cancellation of registration by attaching an authenticated copy or certified copy of the judgment of nullification to the application for cancellation of registration.

    Article 19-8 (Preparation, Keeping, and Management of Registers)
    (1) Upon submission of an application for registration under Article 19-4 (1), the issuing bank shall prepare a register entering matters necessary for registration, including the receipt number, the date of registration, the name and address of the registration right holder, and the cause of registration.
    (2) Matters necessary for the method and procedure for preparing, and for keeping and managing, the register under paragraph (1) shall be prescribed and publicly notified by the Financial Services Commission.

    Article 19-9 (Priority of Rights in Registered Bonds, etc.)
    (1) The priority of rights in registered bonds, etc. shall be determined by the order of registration.
    (2) The order of registration shall be determined by priority number for registrations made in the same column of the register, and by receipt number for registrations made in different columns.
    (3) The priority of a supplementary registration shall follow the priority of its principal registration: Provided, That the order of priority among supplementary registrations relating to the same principal registration shall be determined by the order in which the supplementary registrations are made.

    Article 19-10 (Deposit of Registered Bearer Bonds, etc.)
    When applying Articles 491 (4) and 492 (2) of the Commercial Act and Articles 45 (2) and 84 (2) of the Secured Bond Trust Act to owners of registered bearer bonds, etc., deposit of the registration certificate shall be deemed deposit of the securities or instruments.

